WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.744 --> 00:00:07.874
This is PhishLens, a free and open source tool that checks whether criminals can send email pretending to be your company.

2
00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:16.085
Type your domain and press Scan. PhishLens reads only public records, so there is nothing to install and no sign up.

3
00:00:16.786 --> 00:00:25.746
The live radar shows each check as it runs. SPF, DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS, DNSSEC, blocklists, certificates and more.

4
00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:33.378
In seconds, you get a threat exposure report. One score, a grade, and the attack paths that are still open.

5
00:00:34.078 --> 00:00:39.898
Every area is scored on its own. Hover over a tab, or press Next, to move through them one at a time.

6
00:00:40.599 --> 00:00:46.679
Top risks puts the most serious problems first, and explains in plain English what an attacker could do.

7
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.240
You also see whether you meet the sender rules from Gmail, Yahoo, and Microsoft.

8
00:00:53.430 --> 00:01:01.410
Sign in to monitor your domains. The dashboard tracks your scores, alerts you when a record changes, and reads your DMARC reports.

9
00:01:02.111 --> 00:01:08.791
There are free tools too. A phishing link checker, record checkers and generators, and an email header analyzer.

10
00:01:09.492 --> 00:01:13.672
PhishLens. Know where your domain stands. Scan your domain free, today.
